quickAnswer: "Enter a minimum, a maximum and how many numbers you need, then press Generate. Each number is drawn with crypto.getRandomValues, the browser's cryptographically secure generator, and rejection sampling so every value in the range is exactly equally likely. Turn off duplicates for a draw where no number repeats, such as a raffle."
formula:
  title: "How the Numbers Are Drawn"
  expression: "n = max − min + 1   ·   draw x uniformly from [0, 2³²)   ·   reject x ≥ 2³² − (2³² mod n)   ·   result = min + (x mod n)"
  explanation: "The browser's secure random source gives 32-bit numbers. Taking x mod n directly would make small results slightly more likely whenever n does not divide 2³² evenly (modulo bias), so draws in the uneven top slice are thrown away and redrawn. Every value then has probability exactly 1 ÷ n. Decimals with N places are drawn the same way as whole numbers of 10^−N steps between the minimum and maximum. Without duplicates, each value is drawn at most once (sampling without replacement)."
  variables:
    - name: "n"
      description: "How many different values are possible: max − min + 1 for whole numbers."
    - name: "Rejection sampling"
      description: "Discarding the few raw draws that would bias the result; on average less than one extra draw is needed."
    - name: "Without duplicates"
      description: "You can draw at most n numbers, because after that every value has been used."
workedExamples:
